[5] I remember a time, not too long ago, when a young woman named Emma was struggling to find her place in the world. She felt lost, like she was just going through the motions, and nothing really seemed to matter anymore. But then she started paying more attention to the little things - the way the sun hit her skin, the sound of the birds in the morning, the way the trees looked after a good rain. She started to feel a sense of wonder and awe that she hadn't felt in a while, and it started to bring her back to life.

