[3] If you ever find yourself in the quaint little town of Eldermoor, don't be too quick to judge its quaintness - it has a way of making the most jaded city dweller feel like a child again, and its charm is one of the many reasons you should take a detour on your next road trip. If you do stop in Eldermoor, though, I think you'd find the town's most iconic feature to be the Grand Fountain, a magnificent stone structure that's been the heart of the town for as long as anyone can remember.

