[2] I love to tell stories about the early days of the internet, when it was a wild and untamed frontier, full of promise and peril. If you think the internet today is a mess, just imagine it in the 1990s, when every website had its own custom fonts, and everyone thought they could make a million dollars by selling a share of their company for a few hundred dollars. But I think my personal favorite story from that time is about a young woman named Sarah, who was one of the first to spot the massive potential of e-commerce, back when people still thought you had to have a physical store to be a real business.

If you want to go back even further, to the very origins of the internet, there's a fascinating story about a group of scientists who were working on a project called ARPANET, which was essentially the precursor to the modern internet. They were testing whether they could send messages securely, and one of the first messages ever sent over the internet
