[10] If you've ever watched a sunset on the coast, you know how the light can take on a surreal quality, almost as if the world is being lit from within by some internal fire. One evening, while taking a walk along the beach, I found myself lost in the colors - the deep blues of the water, the golden hues of the sand, and the soft pinks and oranges of the sky. It was as if the world had been given a new lease on life, and all the tension and chaos of the day had melted away, leaving only the simplicity and beauty of the moment.

I thought back to a time in my life when I felt similarly overwhelmed, when the pressures of work and family had left me feeling drained and disconnected. I remember walking along a similar beach, just that day, and feeling a sense of peace wash over me. It was a feeling that came from within, a sense of grounding and purpose that came with being present in the moment. And it was then

