[9] I think my first memory is of going to the fair with my parents when I was six. It was a big one, with all the usual rides and games, but the highlight for me was the big Ferris wheel in the center of the park. My parents let me go up with them, even though they were a bit worried about the height. I remember being a bit nervous, but the view was incredible - you could see the whole fair spread out below you, and the colors and lights were so bright and cheerful that it made my head spin a bit.

But the real highlight was the game they had there with the big stuffed animals. You had to match the animal to its correct picture, and the first one to get it right got a prize. My older brother, who was always a bit of a competitive person<|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|><|im_end|>
