[5] I love to think about the early days of the internet, when it was still a relatively new and mysterious place for many people. If you think back to the late 1990s and the early 2000s, the internet was still a place where you had to be a bit of a tech-savvy person to really make the most of it. But even back then, people were starting to get a sense of the vast possibilities that this new world of online communication and information had to offer.

If you want to go back even further, to the very beginning of the internet as we know it, that's a pretty amazing story too. You have to go back to the Cold War, when the US government was pouring a lot of money into developing this new technology they called the "internet." They were thinking ahead, trying to figure out how they could use this technology to stay ahead of the Soviets, who were also getting into the game and starting to develop their own versions of this
